1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,600
GradeStream
Your DaVinci Resolve grade on the client's phone. Just a link.

2
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:10,500
How it works: Clean Feed monitor → GradeStream on your PC
→ a link → the client's phone

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:15,100
The client installs nothing —
no apps, no accounts

4
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:18,000
Pick the Clean Feed monitor — and you're live

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,600
1. Internet, Wi-Fi or both at once

6
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:21,200
2. A link for the client and a QR code for the room

7
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:23,600
3. The preview is exactly what the client receives

8
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:27,500
Internet, Wi-Fi, or both at once

9
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:32,100
Internet: client in another city, ≈0.2–0.5 s · Wi-Fi: same room, no internet, ≈0.1–0.25 s
Both: each frame is encoded once for everyone

10
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:35,500
Color arrives as a signal —
the same RGB values Resolve outputs

11
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:38,000
Average ΔE2000 0.22 — the visibility threshold is about 1.0

12
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,100
The phone screen is not a reference.
GradeStream is for discussing changes, not final color approval.

13
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:45,300
Notes right on the frame.
1. The client taps the frame and writes a comment

14
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:47,500
2. The marker reaches you: on the preview and over your Clean Feed monitor

15
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:51,600
3. A snapshot of that exact frame and a summary of all comments are saved

16
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:57,000
Scopes for the client: Waveform, Parade, Vectorscope.
Computed on the phone; you decide if they're allowed.

17
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,600
Out of range — the scope frame flashes red:
clipped highlights, crushed blacks, saturation over 100%

18
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:08,600
Vertical video — 1080×1920.
Rotate the Clean Feed monitor in Windows, and the stream is vertical too.

19
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:13,000
Reviewing an edit: sound in sync.
"Smooth & in sync" mode — for directors and producers

20
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:17,100
Measured: median −16…+17 ms,
well inside what viewers can notice (ITU-R BT.1359)

21
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:21,500
Full screen with markers on iPhone — in Safari.
Settings → Apps → Safari → Advanced → Feature Flags → Fullscreen API

22
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,100
Open the link from the messenger in Safari.
Nothing to set up on Android, iPad or a computer.

23
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:31,500
GradeStream — free, open source, Windows 10/11
github.com/ushtozhish/gradestream

